# Data conversion between pebibyte and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between pebibyte and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1PiB to 1024TiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5PiB yields 1536.0TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 0.0009PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TiB yields 0.0014PiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(PiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(PiB))

<<< stdout
1024TiB
1536.0TiB
0.0009PiB
0.0014PiB

<<< stderr
